.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH acc-validate 1  "validate 0.5.4" 
.SH NAME
acc\-validate \- Validate a manifest: schema, timeline, references and recomputed contents
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBacc validate\fR [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Validate a manifest: schema, timeline, references and recomputed contents
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Result format: `text` (the status line, on stderr) or `json` (a result object, on stdout); inferred from the \-\-output extension when omitted
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
text: One status line; `table` is an alias
.IP \(bu 2
json: One JSON object (RFC 8785 bytes) followed by a newline
.RE
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress status lines on stderr
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the result to FILE instead (the status line in text, the object in JSON)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print extra diagnostics on stderr (resolved policy, format, destination, counts). Never changes stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Never color diagnostics. acc\*(Aqs own output is never colored; this and a non\-empty NO_COLOR environment variable switch off color in help and usage errors too
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>
A manifest written by `scan` or `evaluate`, an in\-toto Statement, or JSON Lines of Statements
.SH VERSION
v0.5.4
